<article class="env-proposition" id="C7F8CD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/C7F8CD">Proposition <span data-tag="C7F8CD">5.1.1.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set, and let $\phi : \sCoNerve [S]^{op} \rightarrow \calC $ be an equivalence of simplicial categories. Then there are (canonical) equivalences of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \calP (S) \stackrel{f}{\leftarrow } \calP ''(\phi ) \stackrel{g}{\rightarrow } \calP '(S). \]
</div>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map $f$ was constructed in Proposition <a href="/tag/AAC4A7" data-tag="AAC4A7">4.2.4.4</a>; it therefore suffices to give a construction of $g$. 
    <p>
      Recall that the category $(\sSet )_{/S}$ of simplicial sets over $S$ is endowed model structure, the <em>contravariant</em> model structure defined in §<a href="/tag/76B9C0" data-tag="76B9C0">2.1.4</a>. Moreover, this model structure is simplicial (Proposition <a href="/tag/D31DD9" data-tag="D31DD9">2.1.4.8</a>) and the fibrant objects are precisely the right fibrations over $S$ (Corollary <a href="/tag/87991F" data-tag="87991F">2.2.3.12</a>). Thus, we may identify $\calP '_{\Delta }(S)$ with the simplicial category $(\sSet )_{/S}^{\circ }$ of fibrant-cofibrant objects of $(\sSet )_{/S}$. 
    <p>
      According to Theorem <a href="/tag/4A4E3B" data-tag="4A4E3B">2.2.1.2</a>, the straightening and unstraightening functors $(St_{\phi }, Un_{\phi })$ determine a Quillen equivalence between $(\sSet )^{\calC }$ and $(\sSet )_{/S}$. Moreover, for any $X \in (\sSet )_{/S}$ and any simplicial set $K$, there is a natural chain of equivalences 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  St_{\phi } (X \times K) \rightarrow (St_{\phi } X) \otimes |K|_{Q^{\bullet }} \rightarrow (St_{\phi } X) \otimes K. \]
</div>
    <p>
       (The fact that the first map is an equivalence follows easily from Proposition <a href="/tag/71BCFE" data-tag="71BCFE">3.2.1.13</a>.) It follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/6957FA" data-tag="6957FA">8.3.1.10</a> that $Un_{\phi }$ is endowed with the structure of a simplicial functor, and induces an equivalence of simplicial categories 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (\Set _{\Delta }^{\calC })^{\circ } \rightarrow (\sSet )_{/S}^{\circ }. \]
</div>
    <p>
       We obtain the desired equivalence $g$ by passing to the simplicial nerve. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>